The catalog contains unique `item_code` values, and every event refers to an item present in the catalog. Index the catalog by item code, join each accepted scan event to its catalog section, and sum its units into that section.

An `event_id` may occur more than once. Only its first occurrence in `events` is accepted; every later occurrence with that ID must be ignored, even if its other fields differ. Distinct event IDs are always counted independently.

Return only sections receiving accepted units, ordered lexicographically by section. Empty events produce an empty vector.

Do not include a `main` function. Do not use external packages, filesystem access, networking, clocks, or randomness.","reference_code":"use std::collections::{BTreeMap, HashMap, HashSet};

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct CatalogItem {
    pub item_code: String,
    pub section: String,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct ScanEvent {
    pub event_id: u64,
    pub item_code: String,
    pub units: u32,
}

#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct SectionTotal {
    pub section: String,
    pub units: u64,
}

pub fn units_by_section(
    catalog: &[CatalogItem],
    events: &[ScanEvent],
) -> Vec<SectionTotal> {
    let item_sections: HashMap<&str, &str> = catalog
        .iter()
        .map(|item| (item.item_code.as_str(), item.section.as_str()))
        .collect();
    let mut seen_events = HashSet::new();
    let mut totals: BTreeMap<&str, u64> = BTreeMap::new();

    for event in events {
        if !seen_events.insert(event.event_id) {
            continue;
        }

        let section = item_sections[event.item_code.as_str()];
        *totals.entry(section).or_insert(0) += u64::from(event.units);
    }

    totals
        .into_iter()
        .map(|(section, units)| SectionTotal {
            section: section.to_owned(),
            units,
        })
        .collect()
}
