{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-binary_and_bitwise-rust-generation-02","problem":"Implement `solution.rs` as a standard-library-only Rust library for compactly encoding and decoding controller feature options.

Expose exactly this public API:

```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct FeatureOptions {
    pub emulation: bool,
    pub extended_frames: bool,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum DecodeError {
    ReservedBitsSet,
    ChecksumMismatch,
}

impl FeatureOptions {
    pub fn new() -> Self;
    pub fn set_emulation(&mut self, enabled: bool);
    pub fn set_extended_frames(&mut self, enabled: bool);
    pub fn encode(&self) -> [u8; 2];
    pub fn decode(bytes: [u8; 2]) -> Result<Self, DecodeError>;
}
```

The first encoded byte is a bit mask: bit 0 represents `emulation`, bit 1 represents `extended_frames`, and bits 2 through 7 are reserved and must be zero. The second byte is a checksum computed as `first_byte.rotate_left(1) ^ 0xA7`.

`new` must disable both options. The setters change only their named option. `encode` must produce the exact two-byte representation above. `decode` must reject a first byte containing any reserved bit, returning `ReservedBitsSet` before considering the checksum. For an otherwise valid mask, it must return `ChecksumMismatch` when the checksum byte is incorrect. Valid input must reconstruct the represented options.

Do not use a filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external package, framework, or `main` function.","reference_code":"#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct FeatureOptions {
    pub emulation: bool,
    pub extended_frames: bool,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum DecodeError {
    ReservedBitsSet,
    ChecksumMismatch,
}

impl FeatureOptions {
    pub fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            emulation: false,
            extended_frames: false,
        }
    }

    pub fn set_emulation(&mut self, enabled: bool) {
        self.emulation = enabled;
    }

    pub fn set_extended_frames(&mut self, enabled: bool) {
        self.extended_frames = enabled;
    }

    pub fn encode(&self) -> [u8; 2] {
        let flags = u8::from(self.emulation) | (u8::from(self.extended_frames) << 1);
        [flags, flags.rotate_left(1) ^ 0xA7]
    }

    pub fn decode(bytes: [u8; 2]) -> Result<Self, DecodeError> {
        let flags = bytes[0];
        if flags & !0b0000_0011 != 0 {
            return Err(DecodeError::ReservedBitsSet);
        }
        if bytes[1] != (flags.rotate_left(1) ^ 0xA7) {
            return Err(DecodeError::ChecksumMismatch);
        }
        Ok(Self {
            emulation: flags & 0b0000_0001 != 0,
            extended_frames: flags & 0b0000_0010 != 0,
        })
    }
}
